@Lars 
Yes, except "dry" in this sense does not mean not having water; it means dull, insipid, lacking interest or substance. It would be like using "Having a strong flavor" as a clue for CLEVER. Yes, "sharp" is a synonym of both of those, but they are different meanings.
Pretty lame clue.

